message: "If you use dosen-sim, please cite the preprint and the software as below."
title: "dosen-sim: an agent-based, game-theoretic simulation of lecturer careers in an Indonesian faculty"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Nuhamunada
    given-names: Matin
    email: matin_nuhamunada@ugm.ac.id
version: 0.2.5
date-released: 2026-10-10
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/matinnuhamunada/dosen-sim"
keywords:
  - agent-based modelling
  - game theory
  - academic careers
  - higher education policy
  - Indonesia
abstract: >-
  dosen-sim simulates how Indonesian university lecturers divide their working week between
  teaching, research, community service, supervision, administration, outside work and rest
  under configurable regulations (credit points, workload reporting in SKS, promotion, pay) and
  faculty power dynamics. Rule-based agents choose; a rules engine computes every outcome. The
  main scenario is an anonymised faculty, partly calibrated to aggregate data and the author's
  own (subjective) estimates. Developed with Claude (Anthropic), an AI assistant, under the
  author's direction.
